# Impeccable Design & Polish Rules

## 1. Eliminate "AI Design Tells" (AI Slop)
- NEVER generate uniform 3-column feature grids where every card has a colored circle icon on top, a bold 2-word title, and 2 lines of generic filler text.
- NEVER nest cards inside cards inside cards with heavy shadows.
- NEVER use default Tailwind blue (`#3B82F6`) or purple-to-cyan gradients as brand accents.
- Vary section rhythm: alternate asymmetric 2-column split layouts, clean editorial lists with `1px` dividers, bento grids, and full-bleed visual breaks.

## 2. Color & Surface Discipline (60-30-10 Rule)
- **60% Primary Canvas:** Clean, cohesive background (e.g., warm alabaster `#F8F7F4` or deep obsidian `#0E0F11`).
- **30% Elevated Surfaces:** Subtle tonal shift (`+4%` lightness on dark, `-3%` on light) with crisp `1px` borders to separate cards and panels.
- **10% Single Brand Accent:** One high-contrast accent color reserved strictly for primary CTAs, active states, and key highlights.

## 3. Typographic Precision
- Apply `text-wrap: balance` (`text-balance`) on all `<h1>` and `<h2>` headings to prevent awkward single-word orphans.
- Use `tabular-nums` on all prices, phone numbers, opening hours, and numbered step badges (`01`, `02`, `03`).
- Maintain strict line-length discipline (`max-w-prose` / `55–65ch`) on body copy so text never stretches unreadably across wide monitors.